{{af|ru|сдать|-ва́ть}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|сдава́ть}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-сдавать.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|сдава́ть|impf|pf=сдать}}

# to [[deliver]], to [[hand in]], to [[hand over]]
# to [[return]], to [[turn in]]
#: {{uxi|ru|'''сдава́ть''' [[вещь|ве́щи]] [[в]] [[бага́ж]]|to [[check]]/[[register]] [[one]]'s [[luggage]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[сдава́ть]] [[дело|дела́]]|to [[turn]] [[over]] [[one]]'s [[duties]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''сдава́ть''' [[внаём]]|to [[let]], to [[let out]], to hire out}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''сдава́ть''' [[в]] [[аре́нду]]|to [[lease]], to grant on lease, to [[rent]]}}
# ''(a fortress, city etc.)'' to [[surrender]], to [[yield]]
# {{lb|ru|cards}} to [[deal]]
# to [[take]]/[[pass]] ''(an exam)''
# to [[be]] [[weaken]]ed, to [[be]] [[in]] [[a]] [[reduced]] [[state]]

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|impf|13b|сдава́ть}}

==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{af|ru|с-|дать}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-сдать.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|сдать|pf|impf=сдава́ть}}

# {{lb|ru|transitive}} to [[deliver]], to [[hand in]], to [[hand over]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[учитель|Учи́тель]] [[сказать|сказа́л]] '''сдать''' [[сочинение|сочине́ния]].|The teacher told us to turn in our compositions .}}
# {{lb|ru|transitive}} to [[return]], to [[turn in]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[сдать]] [[вещь|ве́щи]] [[в]] [[бага́ж]]|to [[check]]/[[register]] [[one]]'s [[luggage]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[сдать]] [[дела]]|to [[turn]] [[over]] [[one]]'s [[duties]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[сдать внаем]]|to [[let]], to [[let out]], [[to hire out]]}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[сдать в аре́нду]]|to [[lease]] (out), to [[grant on lease]] (out), to [[rent]] (out)}}
# {{lb|ru|transitive|or|intransitive}} to [[surrender]], to [[yield]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[противник|Проти́вник]] '''сдал''' [[го́род]] [[без]] [[бой|бо́я]].|The enemy surrendered the town without a fight.}}
# {{lb|ru|transitive|or|intransitive|cards}} to [[deal]]
# {{lb|ru|transitive|or|intransitive}} to [[take]]/[[pass]], to usually about an [[exam]]
#: {{uxi|ru|Пе́тька '''сдал''' [[экза́мен]] [[без]] [[особый|осо́бых]] [[усилие|уси́лий]].|Peter passed the exam without much effort.}}
# to [[be]] [[weaken]]ed, to [[be]] [[in]] [[a]] [[reduced state]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[твой|Твой]] [[оте́ц]] [[совсе́м]] '''сдал'''.|Your father's health declined a lot.}}
# to [[move]] [[back]] a [[bit]] (like while driving)
#: {{uxi|ru|[[чтобы|Что́бы]] [[поверну́ть]] ну́жно [[быть|бы́ло]] [[снача́ла]] '''сдать''' [[наза́д]].|In order to turn he first had to ''move backwards a bit''.}}

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|pf|irreg/c+p|сдать|past_n2=сдало́*|notes=* More common but non-standard.}}

==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*mey-|id=change}}
{{inh+|ru|orv|миновати}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*minovati}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|минова́ть}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-миновать.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|минова́ть|both|pf=минова́ть,мину́ть}}

# to [[pass]], to [[elapse]] {{q|of time}}
#* {{RQ:RSB|Mark|6|48|И увидел их бедствующих в плавании, потому что ветер им был противный; около же четвертой стражи ночи подошел к ним, идя по морю, и хотел '''миновать''' их.|t=When he saw that they were straining at the oars against an adverse wind, he came toward them early in the morning, walking on the sea. He intended to '''pass''' them '''by'''. ({{n-g|NRSVUE}})}}
# to [[go by]], to [[go]] [[past]] {{q|without any effect}}
#* '''1848''', {{lw|ru|Давыдов, Дмитрий Павлович|tr=Dmitrij Davydov}}, “Думы беглеца на Байкале (Thoughts of a Runaway in Baikal)”
#*: {{ux|ru|В дéбрях не трóнул прожóрливый зверь,<br>Пу́ля стрелкá — '''миновáла'''.|In the wilderness, the voracious beast bothered [me] not;<br>The shooter's bullet '''passed''' [me] '''by'''.}}
# {{lb|ru|colloquial|or|dated}} to [[turn]] (an age)

====Conjugation====
''imperfective''
{{ru-conj|impf|2a|минова́ть|ppp=-|prpp=-}}
''perfective''
{{ru-conj|pf|2a|минова́ть|ppp=-}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|минова́ть|pf}}

# {{lb|ru|chiefly in the negative}} to [[evade]]
#: {{ux|ru|[[что|Чему́]] [[быть]], [[тот|того́]] [[не]] '''минова́ть'''.|What must be, must be; What happens, happens.}}
# {{lb|ru|intransitive}} to [[end]], to [[finish]]

====Conjugation====
''perfective''
{{ru-conj|pf|2a|минова́ть|ppp=-}}

===Related terms===
* {{l|ru|немину́емый}}, {{l|ru|немину́чий}}
* {{l|ru|размину́ться}}
* {{l|ru|мину́вший}}

{{topics|ru|Time}}

==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*minǫti}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|мину́ть}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|мину́ть|pf|impf=минова́ть}}

# to [[pass]], to [[elapse]] {{gloss|(of time) to pass or move by}}
# to [[go by]], to [[go]] [[past]] (without any effect)

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|pf-intr|irreg|мину́ть}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|мину́ть|pf|impf=минова́ть}}

# to [[turn]] (of age)
#: {{ux|ru|Ему́ '''ми́нуло''' [[со́рок]] лет.|He has turned forty.}}

====Usage notes====
'''мину́ть''' with the meaning "to pass (of time)" or "to go past" can have past stress either {{m|ru|ми́нул}} or {{m|ru|мину́л}}, whereas with the meaning "to turn (an age)" it can only have the past stress as {{m|ru|ми́нул}}. In either case the past active participle is only {{m|ru|мину́вший}}.

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|pf|irreg|мину́ть|root_past_stress=1|ppp=-}}

===Related terms===
* {{l|ru|немину́емый}}, {{l|ru|немину́чий}}
* {{l|ru|размину́ться}}
* {{l|ru|мину́вший}}

